  "overview": {
    "description": "CiapanÃ² (also known as Traversone) is an Italian card game related to Tressette, played mainly in Tuscany and Emilia-Romagna. It is a trick-taking game for 3-5 players where the goal is to avoid taking tricks, similar to the concept of 'misÃ¨re' in other games. The game is the opposite of Tressette in that players try not to win tricks.",
